---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="The Quadratic Formula | Quadratic Equations | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the quadratic formula x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / (2a), its derivation, and step-by-step solved examples for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/quadratic-equations" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Quadratic Equations</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">04</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 04 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS</div>
					<h1>The <span>Quadratic Formula</span></h1>
					<p>
						Learn the universal formula for finding the roots of any quadratic equation ax² + bx + c = 0 easily.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE FORMULA</div>
					<h2>The Quadratic Formula</h2>
					<p>
						For any quadratic equation <em>ax² + bx + c = 0</em> with <em>a ≠ 0</em>, the roots are given by:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / 2a</strong>
						<span>provided that b² - 4ac ≥ 0</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">✓</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Shreedharacharya's Rule</strong>
							<p>
								This formula was historically derived by the ancient Indian mathematician <strong>Sridharacharya</strong> by completing the square on the general equation <em>ax² + bx + c = 0</em>.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · STEP-BY-STEP EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Applying the Formula</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Solve 3x² - 5x + 2 = 0 using the Quadratic Formula</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Identify coefficients</strong>: a = 3, b = -5, c = 2.</p>
							<p><strong>Step 2: Calculate b² - 4ac</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								b² - 4ac = (-5)² - 4(3)(2) = 25 - 24 = <strong>1</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 3: Substitute into the formula</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x = (-(-5) ± √1) / (2 × 3)<br/>
								x = (5 ± 1) / 6
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Taking positive sign: <strong>x = (5 + 1)/6 = 6/6 = 1</strong></p>
							<p>Taking negative sign: <strong>x = (5 - 1)/6 = 4/6 = 2/3</strong></p>
							<p style="margin-top:8px;">Roots are <strong>x = 1</strong> and <strong>x = 2/3</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Solve x² + 4x + 5 = 0 using the Quadratic Formula</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Identify coefficients</strong>: a = 1, b = 4, c = 5.</p>
							<p><strong>Step 2: Calculate b² - 4ac</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								b² - 4ac = (4)² - 4(1)(5) = 16 - 20 = <strong>-4</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Since <em>b² - 4ac = -4 &lt; 0</em>, the square root of a negative number is not a real number.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Conclusion: <strong>No real roots exist</strong> for this equation.
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>The quadratic formula is <strong>x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / (2a)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Always calculate <strong>b² - 4ac</strong> first to check if real roots exist.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Be careful with signs, especially when <em>b</em> or <em>c</em> is negative!</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/quadratic-equations/completing-the-square" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Completing the Square</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/quadratic-equations/nature-of-roots" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Discriminant & Nature of Roots</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">QUADRATIC EQUATIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 04 of 05</div>
